e and honesty is kind of part  of the problem here neither the company  building the pipe  nor any government informed the public  about this spill right after it happened  so we found out about it a month later  so there are questions about  transparency when it comes to future  spills obviously the state is only  required to notify the public if there's  a spill that imminently risks Public  Health and the obvious question is well  according to whose opinion  hasil Minh also added quote it doesn't  give us any pleasure to say I told you  so  but we have said from the beginning that  it's not a matter of if but when  pipelines leak and they spill it's just  what happens Standing Rock Sioux tribe  Chairman Dave R Shambo said quote our  lawsuit challenging this dangerous  project is ongoing and it's more  important than ever for the court to  step in and halt additional accidents  before they happen not just for the  Standing Rock Sioux tribe and our  resources but for the 17 million people  whose drinking water is at risk the  United States is not even benefiting  from this pipeline we're talking about a  foreign company using our natural  resources for oil that is  disproportionately going to go and be  consumed by people in other countries  the risks clearly outweigh even the best  possible potential benefits here and I  will remind you never far behind with  Trump is a potential conflict of  interest Donald Trump was at least at  one point financially connected to the  company that owns or will own the  completed pipeline we have no real  evidence that Trump has severed those  financial ties other than some advisor  at some point saying that Donald Trump  has figured out how to stop the  conflicts of interest or whatever which  quite frankly means nothing to me I mean  it's worth basically dog crap it's of  absolutely no value to us whatsoever
 

